{"stem": "fire_note", "name": "fire_note", "description": "Fire Note \u2014 convert a bare trigger into a music_note note_on event.\n\nA \"cast\" / adapter node: takes a void trigger event and, every time it\nfires, emits a `music_note` struct event carrying the pitch and velocity\ncurrently set on its float params.  This bridges a void event source (e.g. a\nconductor's `beat`, a MIDI/keyboard gate, or a UI button) into a synth's\n`note_on` struct event input, which are otherwise type-incompatible.\n\nExample: conductor.beat (void) -> fire_note.trigger (void)\n         fire_note.note_on (struct music_note) -> mono_synth.note_on\n  plays a note on every beat, at the pitch/velocity dialed in here.\n\nParameters:\n  pitch      [0, 127]  \u2014 MIDI note number (default 60 = middle C)\n  velocity   [0, 1]    \u2014 note-on velocity / amplitude scale (default 1.0)\n\nEvents:\n  trigger (void)               \u2014 fires the note output\n  note_on (struct music_note)  \u2014 emitted each time `trigger` fires, carrying\n                                 the current pitch and velocity values", "sr": 48000, "ch": 1, "build_meta": {"gen_datetime": "2026-07-15 04:07 UTC", "git_commit": "ad6f5fa", "compiled_with": "9d34a62"}, "wasm": "fire_note.wasm", "meta_file": "fire_note.wasm.cragmeta", "meta": {"schema_version": 1, "sample_rate": 48000, "channels": 1, "parameters": [{"name": "pitch", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 127.0, "default": 60.0, "float_index": 0}, {"name": "velocity", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "default": 1.0, "float_index": 1}], "samplers": [], "texture_samplers": [], "events": [{"name": "trigger", "type": "void", "void_index": 0}], "meters": [{"name": "Output", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "float_index": 0}], "event_outputs": [{"name": "note_on", "type": "struct", "fired_index": 0, "value_index": -1, "subtype": "music_note", "struct_type": "music_note", "struct_payload_bytes": 8, "struct_out_byte_offset": 0, "struct_fields": [{"name"